# v1.26 FLEET RETRAIN — the observation contract changed, so the fleet is dead.
#
# WHY. Not a hypothesis, not a price: a BREAK. 4e82807 removed the five
# heard-mission scalars (the leader's mission index and one per subordinate
# slot) and OBS_DIM went 351 -> 346. All nine v1.25 members carry
# torso.0.weight (256, 351) and now fail to load:
#
#   RuntimeError: mat1 and mat2 shapes cannot be multiplied (16x346 and 351x256)
#
# v1.25 cannot be re-evaluated on this tree at all. There is nothing to publish
# and nothing to compare until this campaign lands.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY CHANGED, AND WHAT DID NOT. The doctrine table did NOT change:
# SUB_MISSIONS_BY_SUPERIOR_MISSION has the same 12 keys and the same rows as the
# old DOCTRINE, so the action mask is bit-identical. The rename, the
# Mission.admissible_sub_missions property and the briefing() field are
# publication, not semantics; the README that documented eleven missions was
# simply wrong and is now corrected.
#
# The one behavioural change is the observation, and it is a REMOVAL of
# information in every mode:
#   - voice_only: _note_mission_heard is gone. Overhearing an order no longer
#     teaches a listener which mission a teammate holds. This was a designed
#     channel and it was deleted on purpose (doctrine is common knowledge; what
#     an agent may ORDER never depended on what it had HEARD).
#   - radio modes: those slots were live telemetry. A leader could read the
#     current mission of each of its subordinates. It no longer can.
# Own mission (the MISSION_ORDER one-hot) is untouched.
#
# WHAT TO READ WHEN IT LANDS. The removal takes away exactly what a leader used
# to know about who is already tasked, so the hazard is order churn and the DONE
# loop, not success:
#   retasks_per_episode      up?   (re-ordering a subordinate already on task)
#   obedience_latency_mean   up?
#   closed_on_root_report_rate      the channel v1.25 already reports at 0.01 on
#                                   platoon_hard and 0.58 on platoon
# Success moving is the LEAST interesting outcome here; the reporting axis is
# where a five-scalar removal should show up if it shows up anywhere.
#
# SHAPE. Identical to v1.24: 21 jobs, one frozen cohort/ tree, seed 12 for the
# five scenarios that do not spread, and a DECLARED four-seed search for the
# four that do (squad, platoon, platoon_hard, patrol_brique). Every seed tried
# is listed here and every one goes in seed_search, collapses included — that
# is the rule that keeps this fleet unlaundered.
#
# PRICES ARE THE SHIPPED PRICES. No --reward overrides anywhere in this file.
# done_false stays at -0.5: the platoon_hard done_false=0 arm (3badc83) opened
# the root's DONE channel to 0.824 but bought it with 94 claims an episode at a
# 0.899 false-complete rate and human deaths 0.257 -> 0.404. That is spam, not
# closure, and it is the mirror of squad_v11 at -2.0. Owner decision, this
# session: retrain at the shipped prices.
#
# THE TREE IS FROZEN AT 4e82807 FOR THE DURATION. train.py imports cohort/ at
# the moment each job starts, so a commit to cohort/ mid-campaign trains the
# last members against a different environment and the fleet stops being one
# system. Tooling, tests, docs and boards stay free to move.

fireteam_v16               --scenario fireteam        --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12
fireteam_defend_v27        --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12
squad_v34                  --scenario squad           --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12
